     1	# Agent Implementation Plan
     2	
     3	This repository implements JouleWise, an extensible energy-characterization
     4	benchmark for LLM inference across heterogeneous local hardware. The name is a
     5	nod to JouleSort and Splitwise: energy measurement as the spine, split inference
     6	as the first research application that validates the harness.
     7	
     8	## Ground Rules For Agents
     9	
    10	- At the start of every substantial run, read `RUN_STATE.md` first.
    11	- For any new/random user task, triage it in `TASK_QUEUE.md` before deciding
    12	  whether it outranks the current phase work.
    13	- At the start of each phase or major step, apply
    14	  `docs/planning_reflection_protocol.md` before implementation.
    15	- At the end of every substantial run, update `RUN_STATE.md` and add or update a
    16	  detailed report in `docs/run_reports/`. If advisor-visible state changed (a
    17	  phase or gate closed, a verdict landed, the schedule moved), refresh
    18	  `PROJECT_STATUS.md` too.
    19	- Check `docs/decision_log.md` before re-deciding anything; record new design
    20	  decisions there with options and considerations.
    21	- Per-item phase status is asserted only in
    22	  `docs/phase_N/phase_N_exit_checklist.md` (D-023); this file's checkboxes
    23	  are a coarse mirror updated at slice/phase closes.
    24	- Review `docs/risk_register.md` at phase starts and when a trigger fires.
    25	- Keep run artifacts self-contained and reproducible.
    26	- Prefer small vertical slices that produce complete run bundles.
    27	- Treat unsupported hardware/model combinations as structured outcomes, not
    28	  crashes.
    29	- Keep runtime adapters separate from telemetry adapters.
    30	- Make every result traceable to a config, raw power trace, event log, and
    31	  reducer output.
    32	
    33	## Single Source Of Truth Map
    34	
    35	Detail lives in exactly one place; everything else links to it. When
    36	documents disagree, fix the drift in the same run and note it in the run
    37	report.
    38	
    39	| Artifact | Owns |
    40	|---|---|
    41	| `AGENT_PLAN.md` (this file) | phase index, coarse status mirror, acceptance criteria (per-item status authority: the exit checklists, D-023) |
    42	| `PROJECT_STATUS.md` | advisor-facing status/plan/architecture summary (derived; update when advisor-visible state changes) |
    43	| `docs/phase_N/phase_N_plan.md` | step/slice detail: objectives, design, actions, evidence, fallbacks |
    44	| `docs/phase_N/phase_N_exit_checklist.md` | evidence gates for closing phase N, and per-item status (the authority, D-023) |
    45	| `TASK_QUEUE.md` | what to do next, and why it outranks the rest |
    46	| `docs/agent_playbook.md` | per-mission execution guides for agents: read-first lists, code-level routes, verification, handoff checklists |
    47	| `RUN_STATE.md` | current handoff: state, verification, next step |
    48	| `docs/decision_log.md` | design decisions, options, considerations |
    49	| `docs/risk_register.md` | risks, triggers, mitigations, descope ladder |
    50	| `docs/milestones.md` | calendar constraints and phase target dates |
    51	| `docs/contracts/measurement_methodology.md` | measurement rules (boundaries, clocks, statistics) |
    52	| `docs/contracts/run_bundle_layout.md` | bundle artifact contract |
    53	| `docs/contracts/adapter_contracts.md` | adapter behavior contracts |
    54	| `docs/contracts/node_worker_protocol.md` | remote-execution protocol (transport-independent; pinned during 2K, reused by 2L + Phase 3) |
    55	
    56	Superseded (2026-07-15, WO-021; D-043): `docs/process/state_kernel.json` is the sole editable authority for live work selection, while generated `TASK_QUEUE.md` and `RUN_STATE.md` regions are projections; see `docs/specs/c027/doc-008_state_kernel.md` §§3.1, 3.6, and 4.
    57	
    58	## Canonical Architecture
    59	
    60	```text
    61	typed config
    62	  -> controller
    63	    -> transport adapter: local or ssh
    64	    -> runtime adapter: mlx, vllm, llama.cpp (hailo: unsupported_workload — feasibility finding only)
    65	    -> telemetry adapter: powermetrics, nvidia-smi, jetson rails, wall meter
    66	  -> run bundle
    67	    -> reducers
    68	    -> dashboard / notebooks / report figures
    69	```
    70	
    71	## Phase Index
    72	
    73	### Phase 1: Approval, Feasibility, And Measurement Design
    74	
    75	Status: in progress (most design/feasibility items closed; the remaining
    76	gates need external/hardware input). Detail: `docs/phase_1/phase_1_plan.md`.
    77	Exit: `docs/phase_1/phase_1_exit_checklist.md` (the evidence dossier). The
    78	contracts this phase produced live in `docs/contracts/`.
    79	
    80	- [x] Create repo-local agent plan.
    81	- [x] Add reusable planning reflection protocol.
    82	- [x] Add evidence-based Phase 1 exit checklist.
    83	- [x] Add task queue protocol for prioritizing new work against repo state and
    84	  recent handoffs.
    85	- [x] Define draft typed benchmark config contract.
    86	- [x] Define draft standardized run output contract.
    87	- [x] Define runtime/telemetry/transport adapter interfaces.
    88	- [x] Define run-bundle layout.
    89	- [x] Add example configs for Mac-local and mock-local runs.
    90	- [x] Add schema/interface tests.
